<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Theocracy of Amun at Thebes</h1><p class="st-meta">1080 BCE – 943 BCE (approx.) · capital Thebes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Upper Egypt ruled by the High Priests of Amun at Thebes, who governed through the god's oracle at the end of the New Kingdom.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a> disintegrated under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-xi">Ramesses XI</a>, the general and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-priest-of-amun">High Priest of Amun</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herihor">Herihor</a> took control of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> around 1080 BCE and even wrote his name in a royal cartouche. The country was divided: the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-first-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-first Dynasty of Egypt</a> ruled the north from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanis">Tanis</a> while the high priests held the south.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The high priests were also army commanders, and they ruled from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> in the name of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a>, whose oracle was consulted on appointments, property and justice. They nominally recognised the Tanite kings, and the two houses intermarried. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pinedjem-i">Pinedjem I</a> took royal titles. Faced with tomb robbery, the priests moved the royal mummies to caches such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deir-el-bahari">Deir el-Bahari</a> tomb DB320, where many were found in 1881.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 943 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshenq-i">Sheshonq I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/twenty-second-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-second Dynasty of Egypt</a> installed his own son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iuput-high-priest">Iuput</a> as High Priest, ending the independent theocracy. The office kept great prestige, and power at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thebes">Thebes</a> later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gods-wife-of-amun">God's Wife of Amun</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="theocracy, 1080 BCE – 943 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 82 V46 Q50 12 70 46 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 30 V82 M40 58 H60"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">theocracy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:38.21%;width:2.73%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1080 BCE – 943 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thebes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Herihor, Pinedjem I, Menkheperre</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>High Priests of Amun, Theban theocracy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1012&amp;focus=theocracy-of-amun-at-thebes" aria-label="Theocracy of Amun at Thebes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5543 1232 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Theocracy of Amun at Thebes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5863 1488L5863 1489M5863 1488L5825 1304M5863 1488L5817 1318"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5863 1489h0M5825 1304h0M5817 1318h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5863 1488h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5863 1488h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thebes. <a href="/atlas?year=-1012&amp;focus=theocracy-of-amun-at-thebes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
